The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```java
if (!p.isAlive()) {
```
Reason:
The `Process#isAlive()` method is only available in JDK 8. Since Accumulo 1.8 needs to maintain compatibility with earlier JDK versions, using this method leads to potential failures when checking the status of processes, causing the tests to break.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```java
private boolean isAlive(Process p) {
    try {
        p.exitValue();
        return false;
    } catch (IllegalThreadStateException e) {
        return true;
    }
}
```
Reason:
This custom `isAlive` method checks the process's exit value. If the process has terminated, it returns `false`; if it is still running (throws `IllegalThreadStateException`), it returns `true`. This approach ensures compatibility with earlier JDK versions, thus fixing the bug.

